tasks.brief:
Create only handmetrics/load.py and handmetrics/__init__.py. Do not edit tests/ or data/.

__init__.py must be exactly a package docstring (no re-exports), e.g. """Measure the visual style of handwriting."""

load.py must implement:
  @dataclass
  class Record:
      filename: str
      identity: str
      path: str
  @dataclass
  class Discard:
      filename: str
      reason: str  # 'blank_label' | 'unreadable' | 'missing_image'
  def load(data_dir: str = 'data') -> tuple[list[Record], list[Discard]]:

Behaviour: read {data_dir}/labels.csv (header FILENAME,IDENTITY, no quoting, names may contain spaces). A row is discarded as 'unreadable' if IDENTITY is UNREADABLE, 'blank_label' if IDENTITY is empty/whitespace, 'missing_image' if the JPEG is not present at {data_dir}/images/{FILENAME}. Otherwise it is a Record with path pointing at that JPEG. If a row is both unreadable/blank and missing, missing_image may be used only when the label would otherwise have been usable; unreadable/blank take precedence when the file exists. Counts must be computed by walking the file, never hardcoded. Do not load image pixels.

Satisfy tests/test_load.py. numpy/pillow/pytest only.
